Date: Fri, 6 Mar 2026 09:14:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 23/69] fix(cli): fetch fresh network state so pruned members
 can rejoin (#134)

* fix(cli): fetch fresh network state so pruned members can rejoin when sending messages

Two bugs prevented pruned riverctl members from sending visible messages:

1. send_message_with_key: early is_member check errored before reaching
   build_rejoin_delta, blocking pruned members entirely
2. All storage-based methods (send_message, edit, delete, react, unreact,
   reply, set_nickname): used stale local state where the member still
   appeared present, so build_rejoin_delta never detected pruning

Fix: remove the early is_member gate in send_message_with_key, and fetch
fresh state from the network in all storage-based methods before calling
build_rejoin_delta (matching how the UI uses live-synced state).

Closes #133

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix(cli): improve error message for pruned members without stored credentials

When send_message_with_key is used by a pruned member who has no stored
membership credentials (e.g., never ran `invite accept`), give a clear
error explaining the situation instead of a confusing apply_delta failure.

Also update the docstring to reflect the removed is_member check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

